# Block30 preexecution panel return

This is an author-side five-lens portfolio challenge, not review-loop or an
audit verdict.

| lens | verdict |
|---|---|
| measurement foundations | do not repackage the already-readable equality statistic; test a common successor |
| computational theorem | classify `L_2` under one fixed handoff and stop when both supplied laws survive |
| locality / QCA | a pair-level route can close geometry but cannot stand in for a nearest-neighbor comparison |
| action / gravity | defer the join; the current source has no Record decoder, directed intensity, normalization, or cadence |
| axiom sufficiency | no axiom issue until complete autonomous same-boundary laws disagree or all non-axiomatic routes are exhausted |

The panel selected the output-conditioned handoff unanimously over a signed
one-shot corollary and over an immediate gravity join.  A separate exact scout
then found the displayed four-step family for all 16 ordered exit pairs.  An
independent enumeration confirmed the family and warned that many additional
paths exist, so the block preregisters existence and at-least-two multiplicity,
never global uniqueness.
